      "why": "dual write path: a SECURITY DEFINER rpc (set_note_body(note_id uuid, new_body text)) writes this table AND anon holds a direct INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE grant on it. If the rpc is the intended write path (it holds the validation), the client can skip it and write the table directly -- every RLS assertion still passes. REVOKE the direct DML so the rpc is the only path; the direct-write denial then becomes an assertable boundary."
    },
